1
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:10,820
So, Death Gun was in Laughing
Coffin, and you guys fought before.

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,437
Kirito, I need to know something.

3
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,217
It's about the people you killed.

4
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,300
How did you get over what you did?

5
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,357
How are you not affected by it?

6
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,381
How are you so strong
you're not controlled by it?

7
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:36,680
I haven't gotten over it. What?

8
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:42,780
Last night, I kept having nightmares
about the three guys I killed.

9
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,720
I hardly slept at all.

10
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:48,800
I saw their faces right
before they vanished.

11
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:50,560
I heard their voices.

12
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,780
Their words.

13
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:56,168
I don't think I'm ever
going to forget them.

14
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:58,920
But then...

15
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:01,740
What am I supposed to do?

16
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:03,150
I...

17
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:05,040
I can't...

18
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:06,620
It's okay.

19
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,152
I think that's probably how it should be.

20
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:11,760
I get it now.

21
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:14,017
There are things I shouldn't forget.

22
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:15,580
What it means to kill.

23
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,762
The significance of taking life.

24
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:22,740
And once I accept it, maybe then
I'll be able to find some closure.

25
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,560
That's how I see it.

26
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,110
Closure?

27
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,560
Are you accepting it?

28
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:25,140
I'm not sure what will happen
when I'm going to be a little bit.

29
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:31,700
I'm not sure what I'm going to do.

30
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:37,197
I'm not sure what I'm going to do.

31
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:43,237
I'm not sure what

32
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:45,357
I'm going

33
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:50,577
to do.

34
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:53,080
Believe it,

35
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:55,517
the shodonga hajimari

36
00:02:55,600 --> 00:03:00,320
no oto ni kawarul Yuna.

37
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,937
It's hard to believe
that under that cloak,

38
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:25,961
there's a real-life person
who just wants to kill.

39
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,170
Yeah.

40
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,900
And if I knew his handle in SAO,

41
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:34,024
I'd be able to figure out his name
and address in the real world.

42
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,553
That's the reason why I logged into GGO.

43
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:39,770
Oh.

44
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:44,165
Then, maybe his reason for being
here is because he likes to PK.

45
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:48,040
Maybe he misses the rush of
doing it from SAO. You think?

46
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:50,577
Nah, there's more to it than that.

47
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:54,277
He killed Zekseed and Tarako in
front of a bunch of witnesses.

48
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,242
It was the same with Pale Rider.

49
00:03:57,020 --> 00:04:00,440
He always picks times when
he's got the biggest audience.

50
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:03,260
And that sign of the cross he makes?

51
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:07,073
I bet he does it to freak out
as many people as possible.

52
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:11,197
He wants you to believe he's got the
power to kill you from in the game,

53
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,456
but it's all a show.

54
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:15,487
If that's true, then
how's he killing people?

55
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:18,497
It's not because of brain
damage from their headgear.

56
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:22,462
The authorities said that Zexeed
and Tarako died of heart failure.

57
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:24,820
Heart failure?

58
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,160
My god.

59
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:30,900
To be honest, I have no idea
how he killed him either.

60
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:36,337
But the thought of firing a gun in the
virtual world and stopping a player's heart?

61
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:38,244
There's no way that's possible.

62
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:40,940
Hang on a second.

63
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:43,480
Come to think of it. What?

64
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:46,280
That was weird. What was?

65
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,197
Back there in the ruins.

66
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:52,157
He had his handgun out for you, but
he switched to the rifle for me.

67
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,080
But he kills with the handgun.

68
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,762
He could have killed me with it.

69
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,320
So why'd he switch?

70
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:00,700
Yeah, good question.

71
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:14,145
Could it be that he didn't shoot me with
it because he couldn't shoot me with it?

72
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:17,237
The handgun.

73
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,760
Can't use it, though. The switch.

74
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,740
The crossing-himself thing.

75
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:24,800
Invisibility cloak. Conditions. Rules.

76
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:27,050
Phew.

77
00:05:27,133 --> 00:05:30,884
I can't tell you how relieved I
am to hear you put it into words.

78
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,430
Knew it.

79
00:05:34,513 --> 00:05:36,337
In-game guns can't kill IRL.

80
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:38,957
Shooting someone from in
here is not what does it.

81
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,275
It takes preparation.

82
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,600
Now you lost me.

83
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:45,097
The only way to make it look
like he's killing people in

84
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:48,880
-game is by setting up for the
murder in the real world first.

85
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,557
How would he set something like that up?

86
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:56,720
I mean, if you're right, he'd have to get
a player's real-life information to do it.

87
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,862
All that stuff's secure, though.

88
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,690
No.

89
00:06:01,773 --> 00:06:06,220
If someone's clever enough, they can
find out a player's address easy. How?

90
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:07,740
The terminals.

91
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,657
At the governor's office.

92
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:10,570
Yes.

93
00:06:10,653 --> 00:06:13,537
You have to plug your real name
and address into him to compete.

94
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:14,960
It's an open space.

95
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:17,081
You don't have any privacy there.

96
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,310
No way.

97
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:22,037
You saying he peeked over their
shoulders while they entered their info?

98
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:26,017
That can't be it, because you'd
notice someone lurking next to you.

99
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:29,537
He could have used a scope or some
binoculars from across the room.

100
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:30,817
That's breaking etiquette.

101
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:33,782
He'd get his ass kicked
out of the game for that.

102
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:39,397
Then how about this
maybe death gun can like

103
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:42,068
use his cloak to turn
invisible in town too?

104
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:48,937
He'd be right there and you wouldn't
even know it but still he can't do

105
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:53,785
anything in The real world when he's logged
in here he's unconscious there right?

106
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:03,137
Wait. That's it? Yeah.

107
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,557
It's not just him.

108
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:06,780
Death Gun has a partner.

109
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,220
Check it out.

110
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:12,040
One of them plays as the Death Gun avatar.

111
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:14,160
His job is to shoot the target.

112
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:18,897
At the same time in the real world, the
second person's in the target's apartment.

113
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,980
His job is to take the player out.

114
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,660
Okay, but let's say they
found out your address.

115
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,777
What about the other people living there?

116
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:31,154
And they'd need a key.

117
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,600
As far as Zexeed and Tarako go,

118
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:37,646
they lived alone, and their
apartments were in older buildings.

119
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:42,160
The E-locks on their doors were
probably first-gen, not very secure.

120
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:43,850
Besides,

121
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,757
they were both diving in
GGO during the break-in,

122
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:49,557
so they were both unconscious
and completely helpless.

123
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:53,464
They couldn't hear, so the killer
could take his time getting in.

124
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:58,097
But then, you said the cause of death
for both was heart failure, right?

125
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,557
So how'd they stop someone's
heart in a way both

126
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,117
the cops and the coroner
couldn't figure out?

127
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:06,141
Maybe by injecting some
kind of drug or something?

128
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,360
That's one way.

129
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:10,760
Okay, but someone should
have found evidence of it.

130
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,140
A mark or something.

131
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:17,277
They didn't find the bodies for a
while, so they were pretty decomposed.

132
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:21,419
Besides, a hardcore gamer can go
for days without eating or sleeping.

133
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:26,502
I doubt anyone would think it's weird if
someone died of a heart attack after that.

134
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,020
They're crazy!

135
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:30,610
Right?

136
00:08:30,693 --> 00:08:33,140
I mean, why else would anyone do this?

137
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,270
Maybe.

138
00:08:35,353 --> 00:08:39,140
Or maybe they do it because red
players are who they really are.

139
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:44,000
I mean, deep down, I think
I'm really a swordsman.

140
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:47,280
When you put it that way,
I can sort of understand.

141
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:50,867
There's times when I
think I'm a real sniper.

142
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:51,940
Not a gamer.

143
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:57,660
Wait, do you think the guy doing
the killings is a red player too?

144
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:59,800
You know, like Death Gun?

145
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:03,398
Yeah, they were probably in
Laughing Coffin together.

146
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:06,577
I'm still wondering how
they coordinated the

147
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,177
killings between this
world and the real one.

148
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:11,260
How were they so precise about it?

149
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,360
Yeah, that's it.

150
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,217
That's what doing the Sign
of the Cross is about.

151
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,657
It's not just for show.

152
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:22,211
It's also a great opportunity
to sneak a peek at his watch.

153
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,020
You're right.

154
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,000
Sinon, do you live alone?

155
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,900
Yeah, but I'm sure I locked my door.

156
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:43,000
My building's got first-gen
locks, but I've also got a chain.

157
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:46,216
I think I left the chain off tonight.

158
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,000
Oh, man.

159
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:53,160
Listen, you're not gonna like this.

160
00:09:56,080 --> 00:10:01,260
When Death Gun was chasing us on that
horse, I wasn't the one he was shooting at.

161
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:06,087
And that could only mean they got their
next victim all set up and ready to go.

162
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,880
Okay, then who's next?

163
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:13,120
I got a feeling that right
now in the real world,

164
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,177
Death Gun's partner's in your place.

165
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:19,554
He's watching the live stream, waiting
for when you get shot by that gun.

166
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,200
It's just a hunch.

167
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:01,957
No! No!

168
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,360
No, not that! Oh, God!

169
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:20,930
Calm down.

170
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:23,693
If you log out now, you'll be in danger.

171
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:25,100
Just calm down.

172
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,520
Go easy.

173
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:41,942
Until Death Gun shoots you, the guy in your
place isn't going to do anything, okay?

174
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:44,969
That's the rule they
set up for themselves.

175
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:49,940
But if you log out now and wake up
with his partner there, he'll kill you.

176
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,260
So you have to calm down.

177
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,640
But, but, I'm scared.

178
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,000
I'm so scared.

179
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:09,660
Jeez, Chris Head.

180
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,395
Took you long enough.

181
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,590
Sorry, guys.

182
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:17,371
I booked it over here as fast
as I could for my save point.

183
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:21,952
If there were a speed limit in ALO, my
license would have gotten suspended.

184
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,030
Huh?

185
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:27,640
What is going on?

186
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:37,406
I'd be happy to explain in detail, but I
should warn you, it might take a while.

187
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:40,457
To tell the truth, I'm not
100 % sure where to begin.

188
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:41,422
Oh, don't even.

189
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:42,900
Not to worry.

190
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:44,648
I know just where to start.

191
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,040
On November 9th, in Gun Gale Online,

192
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:53,007
a player called Death Gun fired his weapon
at an avatar appearing on a monitor.

193
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:58,000
That same day, in Nakano Ward, the
player of that avatar mysteriously died.

194
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,880
Young lady, that was unbelievable.

195
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:09,577
Gathering all that information
and connecting it so quickly,

196
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:11,601
you must be quite the researcher.

197
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:14,597
Have you ever thought about
a career in the VR section?

198
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,660
Whoa, you win. I'm sorry.

199
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:19,097
I'm not going to stonewall you, promise.

200
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:20,945
Just complimenting her is all.

201
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:22,817
She's right, though.

202
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:23,730
It's true.

203
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:25,768
Yo, Chris Heider, whatever.

204
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:29,357
I hear you're the one that hired
Kirito to dive into that game.

205
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,717
So let me get this straight.

206
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,797
You got him to convert
over knowing a player

207
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,497
got shot in-game and
died IRL because of it?

208
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,280
Easy, Klein, I can explain.

209
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:39,157
That's not how the player died.

210
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,120
Then how?

211
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,340
It's not the Amusphere rig.

212
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:45,897
No matter what happens to you
in-game, it can't hurt you.

213
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:48,197
And it certainly can't
stop a player's heart

214
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:50,437
when it's not even
directly connected to it.

215
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:51,437
As a matter of fact,

216
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:53,497
Kirito and I met last week to talk about

217
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:56,137
it and pretty much
agreed it was impossible.

218
00:13:56,220 --> 00:14:01,044
There's no way anyone can kill a person
in real life by shooting them in the game.

219
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:04,250
Okay, then.

220
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:09,146
If what you say is true, how come you had
my brother dive into GGO for you, huh?

221
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,678
You had a hunch something was wrong.

222
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:12,890
Scratch that.

223
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,608
You know something's wrong.

224
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:16,697
That Death Gun guy's a part of it.

225
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:19,839
And I bet you sent my brother
in to try to find him.

226
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:23,600
Chris Height, we figured it out.

227
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,957
Death Gun is an SAO survivor just like us.

228
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,460
But unlike us,

229
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:32,797
he was a red player who was in a guild
of killers called Laughing Coffin.

230
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,500
You sure he was with them?

231
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:36,110
Yes.

232
00:14:36,193 --> 00:14:38,072
None of us can remember his name, though.

233
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:41,908
Klein and I met him once, when
our group went to capture his.

234
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:43,720
Um, hey, Asuna.

235
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,037
I get the feeling Chris Height
knows more than he's letting on.

236
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,517
No offense, Chris Height,

237
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:51,717
but all we know is you work for the
government doing something with networks.

238
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:57,280
and that you play ALO as part of some
kind of research you're doing on VR Miss.

239
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,440
Only for the past year.

240
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:03,220
The job I had before was
a little... different.

241
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:07,520
I used to be part of the task
force for the SAO incident.

242
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:13,561
But even though we were called a task force,
in the end, we were pretty ineffective.

243
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:18,417
Chris Height, you're obviously
well-connected, and with a little digging,

244
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:22,557
you could find out what the real-life
name and address of this death gun is.

245
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:26,517
Just make a list of the handles of all
the surviving Laughing Coffin members,

246
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:28,180
then contact their ISPs,

247
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:30,397
ask which one's playing GGO now?

248
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:31,951
and trace their location.

249
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:34,064
No, sorry, that's not possible.

250
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,617
The ISPs aren't going to
give out a player's real

251
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:39,757
-life info if all we have
to go on are their handles.

252
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:42,597
Maybe if we ask the game's
admins, they could help.

253
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:45,277
They might, but GGO's
admins are in the U .S.,

254
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,948
so it'll be a while
before we got an answer.

255
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,720
I know my brother.

256
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:54,297
And right now, he's risking
his life in that game,

257
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:56,615
trying to find out who this person is.

258
00:15:56,820 --> 00:16:01,702
When he came home last night, he had this
look on his face, like he'd seen a ghost.

259
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,647
He must have bumped into the guy
yesterday during the prelims.

260
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:10,300
I bet that's when he realized someone
from Laughing Coffin was in GGO.

261
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,871
Someone who figured out how to
kill players for real again.

262
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:18,638
My brother went back to put
an end to that nightmare.

263
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:22,580
To find out his name and stop
his PK-ing once and for all.

264
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:24,980
Darn it, Kirito.

265
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,984
You should have said something.

266
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:28,410
Why?

267
00:16:28,493 --> 00:16:30,040
Why do you always do this?

268
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,440
That damn idiot.

269
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:34,388
Why didn't he say anything?

270
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:36,437
I could be backing him up right now.

271
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:39,337
All he had to do was ask and I
would have converted over too.

272
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:40,479
We all would have.

273
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,840
Don't you see?

274
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:43,517
That's why he didn't tell us.

275
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,497
If he thought there was any real
danger in what he was doing,

276
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:49,345
There's no way he'd get
us mixed up in it, too.

277
00:16:49,540 --> 00:16:50,834
That's just how he is.

278
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:52,557
Yeah, you're right.

279
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:55,111
He always thinks of others before himself.

280
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,777
In fact, he's probably
protecting someone right now.

281
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:01,742
And whoever that is, I bet it's
someone who doesn't like him much.

282
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,200
Okay, Chris Head, where
is Kirito diving from?

283
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:12,029
I know you know, so
you better tell me now.

284
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:14,896
That's confidential.

285
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:17,780
Okay, okay.

286
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:18,900
I'll tell you.

287
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:21,480
I set up the room myself, so he's safe.

288
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,677
Security's rock solid, and the
monitoring's top of the line.

289
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:27,857
I've got a trained professional
right by his side at all times,

290
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,877
and I guarantee that his body's
in no danger whatsoever of…

291
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:31,790
Where is he?

292
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:33,910
A hospital.

293
00:17:33,993 --> 00:17:37,340
It's in Ocho no Miss, in
Chiyoda Ward. He's in Chiyoda?

294
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:41,457
Wait, is that the same hospital he
was in during his rehabilitation?

295
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:42,937
Yes, that's the one.

296
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,540
I'm going over there.

297
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:47,878
I want to see him, and you
can't do a thing about it.

298
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,940
Tell me you got a plan.

299
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:59,260
We're going to take out Death Gun.

300
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:03,020
Once we do, his real-world
partner will stand down.

301
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:05,396
Then he'll just leave your apartment.

302
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,660
Okay, but he's skilled.

303
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,820
Black Star or no Black Star.

304
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:14,881
You saw, he dodged Hecate's bullet
from just a hundred meters away.

305
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:19,740
And besides, I can't hide in
this cave forever, you know?

306
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:24,157
By now, the other players probably
figured out the two of us are in here.

307
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:26,217
We might as well be sitting ducks.

308
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:29,937
It's just a matter of time before
someone tosses a grenade in.

309
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:30,850
You're right.

310
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:34,024
We've been a team this
whole time anyway, right?

311
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,321
Might as well finish it together.

312
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:40,668
Okay, but there's still the risk
he shoots you with that gun.

313
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:42,142
Oh, that thing?

314
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,977
It's just an old-school
single-action sidearm.

315
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:48,060
He can fire it all he
wants, but I got you there.

316
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:50,477
Just deflect the bullets with your sword.

317
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:53,537
Right, and I won't let a
single one of them hit you.

318
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:56,697
I still don't feel good about
you being out there, though.

319
00:18:56,780 --> 00:19:00,237
I mean, Death Gun's dangerous, and
you shouldn't get too close to him.

320
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:02,300
Oh, come on. Hang on.

321
00:19:02,540 --> 00:19:06,397
I'm totally cool with you fighting with
me, and I wouldn't have it any other way.

322
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:09,060
But, Sinon, you're a sniper, remember?

323
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,877
Isn't your specialty
the long-range attack?

324
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:12,790
Well, yeah.

325
00:19:12,873 --> 00:19:13,780
What about it?

326
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:15,281
Here's the plan.

327
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,837
On the next scan, I'm going to
step outside so it picks me up.

328
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:21,317
That way, we'll get
Death Gun to come to us.

329
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:23,857
He'll probably keep his
distance and take cover.

330
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:26,557
Then he'll try to pick
me off with his rifle.

331
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:30,157
When he shoots, we'll know where
he is, and then you take him out.

332
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:31,299
What do you think?

333
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,280
Are you cool with playing
the decoy? Mm-hmm.

334
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:37,420
Alright, we do it your way then.

335
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:39,217
Just be careful out there,

336
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:43,006
cause if he drops you with his
first shot, I'm gonna be pissed.

337
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,637
I'll keep that in mind.

338
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,132
Wait, I just remembered.

339
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:51,737
His rifle's got a silencer and you won't
see the bullet line on the first shot.

340
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:53,597
Oh, I'll just predict the prediction.

341
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:56,327
You know, like a certain
no-good faker told -

342
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:59,420
Um, I think we should stop talking.

343
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:05,517
Oh, crap.

344
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,837
We should have been paying more attention.

345
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:08,840
What is it?

346
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,700
And will it kill us?

347
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:12,560
It's a live stream camera.

348
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:16,417
Usually, they're only supposed to
shadow players on the battlefield.

349
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:20,377
I guess this one's in here now, because
there aren't many of us left out there.

350
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:23,320
Then do you think it hurt us?

351
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:24,660
Not a chance.

352
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:28,417
For it to pick us up, we'd have to
be shouting at the top of our lungs.

353
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,735
Wave to the audience.

354
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:34,206
Unless you got someone back at
home you don't want seeing this.

355
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:40,597
Uh, I, um, shouldn't you
be worried who's watching?

356
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:43,877
I mean, since I sort of look like
a girl, they might, you know,

357
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,313
think you're, you know.

358
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,200
Well, I don't care.

359
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,717
They can think what they want.

360
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:50,337
The guys in this game are dorks.

361
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:54,257
If they think I'm gay, at least they'll
stop hitting on me every five seconds.

362
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:57,437
How much longer am I going to have
to keep pretending to be a girl?

363
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:58,880
Oh, you poor baby.

364
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,477
You've been faking it like
a champ since you logged in.

365
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,501
Another hour or two won't matter.

366
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,110
Thank God.

367
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,120
We better get ready.

368
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:12,688
We got two minutes
before the next SAT scan.

369
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:14,240
I'll set up here.

370
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:19,325
When you get outside, fire up your terminal
and let me know when our boy's close.

371
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,540
Wait. Hold on.

372
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:26,320
Why? What's wrong?

373
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:28,916
It's too late to change the plan now.

374
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:30,210
No.

375
00:21:30,293 --> 00:21:31,937
I don't want to change anything.

376
00:21:32,020 --> 00:21:33,137
It's something else.

377
00:21:33,220 --> 00:21:36,660
I was just thinking about
Death Gun's real handle here.

378
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:40,277
The only name you didn't recognize
who's still alive is Sterben.

379
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,360
Oh, huh.

380
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:43,112
I guess that's him then.

381
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:46,405
I wonder why he gave
himself that name, though.

382
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:50,665
If I get up close and personal,
I'll be sure to ask him for you.

383
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:54,560
Well, here goes nothing.

384
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:58,620
Be careful, okay?

385
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:08,660
I would like to be strong, strong.

386
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:14,740
I would like to say that
the sadness will be.

387
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:17,637
I never felt like

388
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:22,157
it

389
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:26,877
was a long time. I was
not lost in the past.

390
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:29,777
I was not lost in the past.

391
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:31,317
I could have been a long time.

392
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:34,117
I can't see anything you can see.

393
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:38,577
I can't see anything that's all?

394
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:41,317
I can't see anything else.

395
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:45,157
I can't see anything alone.

396
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:48,797
If I can't see anything else?

397
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:51,940
I don't need anything else. Oh.
